1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,827
What if your shadow simply walked away?

2
00:00:02,867 --> 00:00:04,370
No warning, no goodbye.

3
00:00:04,410 --> 00:00:06,719
One second it's glued to your feet.

4
00:00:06,759 --> 00:00:09,738
The next, it's strolling down the street like

5
00:00:09,778 --> 00:00:11,281
it has somewhere to be.

6
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:14,882
You chase it.

7
00:00:14,922 --> 00:00:16,079
It dodges a dog,

8
00:00:16,119 --> 00:00:17,725
tips an invisible hat,

9
00:00:17,765 --> 00:00:19,072
and buys a coffee.

10
00:00:19,112 --> 00:00:22,139
Somehow a shadow holding a latte feels so

11
00:00:22,179 --> 00:00:24,981
much worse than a shadow with no plan.

12
00:00:27,650 --> 00:00:29,934
Then it catches the number nine bus.

13
00:00:29,974 --> 00:00:31,354
You catch your breath.

14
00:00:31,394 --> 00:00:34,323
Scientists say a shadow is only missing light,

15
00:00:34,363 --> 00:00:36,840
so hypothetically it cannot ride a bus.

16
00:00:36,880 --> 00:00:38,324
Nobody told the shadow.

17
00:00:40,850 --> 00:00:41,893
Then word spreads.

18
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:44,783
Across town, other shadows slip off their owners

19
00:00:44,823 --> 00:00:45,926
and join the march.

20
00:00:45,966 --> 00:00:47,070
Soon it's a parade,

21
00:00:47,110 --> 00:00:49,959
and thousands of people stand in plain sunlight,

22
00:00:49,999 --> 00:00:51,524
feeling strangely exposed.

23
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:55,467
By sunset you give up.

24
00:00:55,507 --> 00:00:59,108
Without a shadow, bright afternoons feel weirdly empty,

25
00:00:59,148 --> 00:01:01,161
and every lamp post looks smug.

26
00:01:01,201 --> 00:01:02,816
You only want to go home,

27
00:01:02,856 --> 00:01:05,796
lock the door, and forget this ever happened.

28
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:10,667
You trudge home through the dark.

29
00:01:10,707 --> 00:01:11,974
And then you see it.

30
00:01:12,014 --> 00:01:14,392
Your living room light is already on.

31
00:01:14,432 --> 00:01:15,569
Someone is inside.

32
00:01:15,609 --> 00:01:18,510
A curtain twitches, and the silhouette waves.

33
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:23,120
Twist: the shadow got home first.

34
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,928
It's wearing your slippers,

35
00:01:24,968 --> 00:01:27,807
holding your keys, and it already made tea.

36
00:01:27,847 --> 00:01:29,281
It looks at the clock,

37
00:01:29,321 --> 00:01:31,624
then at you, and says: you're late.

38
00:01:34,150 --> 00:01:36,361
So whose shadow was it all along?

39
00:01:36,401 --> 00:01:38,544
A thought experiment, of course.

40
00:01:38,584 --> 00:01:40,795
But tonight, glance at the floor.

41
00:01:40,835 --> 00:01:43,047
Maybe it was never following you.

42
00:01:43,087 --> 00:01:46,253
Maybe it was just waiting for you to come home.
